From 43cb700f697aad1aa2ed693bad637eca417ad016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:12:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): book a host reboot as host_reboot, block the
 card whose sudo shutdown caused it [daveey]

2026-10-29, hermes-hub: a worker's test subprocess ran `sudo -n /sbin/shutdown -r now` from its workspace.
The dead-worker sweep booked every running card `crashed` ("pid N not alive"), counted a failure on each,
and retried the culprit, which rebooted the hub twice more (self-heal kanban-f6d16c4695).

Every spawn already records worker_started_at = "<boot_id>:<pid1 start>|<start>". In _reclaim_dead_workers,
when that boot id differs from the current one (both known), the worker died with its host:
- the run outcome and event are `host_reboot`, and a bystander is requeued WITHOUT counting a failure;
- hermes_cli/kanban_host_reboot.py reads the spawn boot's journal (`journalctl -b <boot> _COMM=sudo`,
  cached per boot) for an executed shutdown/reboot/poweroff/halt/systemctl reboot. If its PWD is in the
  card's workspace (or a path naming the card id), or in the assignee profile's scratch dir while the card
  is that profile's only reboot victim, the card is the culprit: tripped at once with block_kind
  `capability`, the journal line in last_failure_error, and a comment on it and its linked cards.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_host_reboot.py (journal parsing, boot compare, workspace culprit +
bystander, profile-scratch sole victim, two victims -> neither blocked, plain reboot -> all requeued
uncounted, same-boot death still `crashed`). 4 integration tests fail without the dispatcher change.
Replayed on the real hub runs: 5623/5633 (workspace) and 5639 (bb-tuner scratch) -> host_reboot + blocked;
bystanders 5629/5634 -> host_reboot, uncounted.

Public-series adaptation: also carries source merge-only resolutions and restores
respawn-guard regression tests and the stalled stripe trace field omitted by
earlier curated patches. See mirror-958-verification.md for the exact inventory.

